1️⃣ Maximum Depth of Binary Tree — LeetCode #104 ⭐
class Solution {
    public int maxDepth(TreeNode root) {

        if (root == null) {
            return 0;
        }

        int left = maxDepth(root.left);
        int right = maxDepth(root.right);

        return 1 + Math.max(left, right);
    }
}

Concept: Recursion

        1
       / \
      2   3
     /
    4

Maximum depth = 3

Time: O(n)
Space: O(h)

2️⃣ Same Tree — LeetCode #100
class Solution {
    public boolean isSameTree(TreeNode p, TreeNode q) {

        if (p == null && q == null) {
            return true;
        }

        if (p == null || q == null) {
            return false;
        }

        if (p.val != q.val) {
            return false;
        }

        return isSameTree(p.left, q.left)
            && isSameTree(p.right, q.right);
    }
}
🧠 Logic

First:

p.val == q.val

Then recursively check:

left == left
right == right
3️⃣ Invert Binary Tree — LeetCode #226 ⭐⭐
class Solution {
    public TreeNode invertTree(TreeNode root) {

        if (root == null) {
            return null;
        }

        TreeNode temp = root.left;
        root.left = root.right;
        root.right = temp;

        invertTree(root.left);
        invertTree(root.right);

        return root;
    }
}

